                <pb facs="0381" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/526: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-31T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                                1927—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 31—10:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>307. Following additional information American consul at Swatow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“All Americans in outlying districts now concentrated and being held in
                            Swatow except six Catholic missionaries in Kay [garbled group] district;
                            they have been urged to leave. Local conditions remain quiet.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
